# A read inside a list whose storage holds raw doubles or int32s loads, asks for the hole and calls nothing, as a read out of boxed storage does. It was held to what the schema declares for every read by position:
# it may throw and may collect. So the sweep kept it where nobody used it, and a loop that only counts read its list in every turn.
# Where the contents are claimed to be fewer numbers than all, the read holds the double against that claim and may stop: there it stays.
# f1 = turn
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: level=Proven
# CHECK: Return
# RUN(RUNS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.id = value => value; globalThis.report = value => print(String(value));
